  "abstract": "This is the second experiment in my systematic ablation of the SOTA architecture. The previous ablation (ID 520) showed that reducing the `residual_hidden` dimension was detrimental. This experiment tests the `residual_scale` hyperparameter, which controls the magnitude of the input-adaptive modulation. I hypothesize that a smaller, more subtle modulation might be more stable and improve performance. I am reducing this parameter from 0.05 (\u00b15%) to 0.025 (\u00b12.5%), with all other aspects of the SOTA architecture held constant for a controlled comparison.",
